menu "UI Component Configuration"

    config UI_DEEP_SLEEP_COUNTDOWN_SEC
        int "Deep sleep countdown duration (seconds)"
        default 30
        range 10 300
        help
            Duration in seconds for countdown timer from light sleep to deep sleep.
            This timer starts when the system enters light sleep and triggers
            transition to deep sleep when it expires.

            Recommended: 30-60 seconds for battery-powered devices.

    config UI_LIGHT_SLEEP_TICK_MS
        int "LVGL tick period in light sleep (milliseconds)"
        default 100
        range 50 1000
        help
            LVGL timer tick period when in light sleep mode.
            Slower tick reduces CPU usage and power consumption.
            Default is 100ms (vs 10ms in active mode).

    config UI_MOON_ANIM_ENABLE
        bool "Play boot animation of the last synodic moon month"
        default y
        help
            On boot, sweep the moon through the last synodic month
            (29.53 days) and settle on the current phase. Each frame is
            one full-resolution moon_bake, identical to the static
            frame; a dedicated task bakes them row by row in the
            background while the display shows each frame as a
            top-to-bottom sweep of 25-row strips, so frames appear one
            after the other with no gaps. The idle->sleep timer is held
            for the sweep so it completes before the device may sleep.

    config UI_MOON_ANIM_FRAMES
        int "Boot animation frame count (1-2 per day)"
        default 28
        range 5 60
        help
            Number of full-resolution frames in the boot animation,
            evenly spaced over the last synodic month: 28 = one frame
            per day (a ~28 s sweep), 56 = two frames per day. Each
            frame sweeps in over its ~1 s bake time (row-parallel
            pipeline), so higher counts are smoother without freezing
            the display.

    config UI_MOON_ANIM_ON_WAKE
        bool "Replay the moon animation on every wake from sleep (testing)"
        default n
        help
            Test hook: whenever the device wakes from sleep back to the
            main screen, replay the boot animation over the last
            synodic month. Lets the sweep be exercised repeatedly
            without a reboot. Off in normal builds.

    config UI_IMU_ENABLE
        bool "Drive the moon spin from the QMI8658 IMU (device tilt)"
        default y
        help
            In normal modes the in-plane moon angle follows the
            device's screen-plane roll (QMI8658 gravity vector), so
            tilting the device turns the moon "ball in hand". Touch
            drag still works and adds to the tilt angle. When the IMU
            is absent or this is disabled the moon is static and only
            drag spins it.

    config UI_IMU_ANGLE_SIGN
        int "IMU angle sign (+1 or -1, flips the spin direction)"
        default 1
        range -1 1
        help
            The board's IMU mounting orientation is board-specific; if
            tilting the device turns the moon the "wrong" way, set this
            to -1.

    config UI_IMU_ROLL_OFFSET_DEG
        int "IMU roll offset (degrees, aligns the resting orientation)"
        default 0
        range 0 359
        help
            Added to the gravity angle so a chosen resting orientation
            of the device maps to a chosen moon spin angle. 0 = the
            gravity angle is used as-is.

endmenu
